@anon.8ad231a129453d088979dfad2582f60a.1118 = private unnamed_addr constant [706 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of Airflow functions and values that have been moved to its providers\0Abut still have a compatibility layer (e.g., `apache-airflow-providers-standard`).\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AAirflow 3.0 moved various deprecated functions, members, and other\0Avalues to its providers. Even though these symbols still work fine on Airflow 3.0,\0Athey are expected to be removed in a future version. The user is suggested to install\0Athe corresponding provider and replace the original usage with the one in the provider.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom airflow.operators.python import PythonOperator\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom airflow.providers.standard.operators.python import PythonOperator\0A```\0A", align 1
