@anon.8ad231a129453d088979dfad2582f60a.1149 = private unnamed_addr constant [703 x i8] c"## Removed\0AThis rule has been removed because type checkers can infer this type without annotation.\0A\0A## What it does\0AChecks that class method `cls` arguments have type annotations.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AType annotations are a good way to document the types of function arguments. They also\0Ahelp catch bugs, when used alongside a type checker, by ensuring that the types of\0Aany provided arguments match expectation.\0A\0ANote that many type checkers will infer the type of `cls` automatically, so this\0Aannotation is not strictly necessary.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```python\0Aclass Foo:\0A    @classmethod\0A    def bar(cls): ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0Aclass Foo:\0A    @classmethod\0A    def bar(cls: Type[\22Foo\22]): ...\0A```\0A", align 1
