@anon.8ad231a129453d088979dfad2582f60a.1157 = private unnamed_addr constant [807 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks that private functions and methods have return type annotations.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AType annotations are a good way to document the return types of functions. They also\0Ahelp catch bugs, when used alongside a type checker, by ensuring that the types of\0Aany returned values, and the types expected by callers, match expectation.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef _add(a, b):\0A    return a + b\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef _add(a: int, b: int) -> int:\0A    return a + b\0A```\0A\0A## Availability\0A\0ABecause this rule relies on the third-party `typing_extensions` module for some Python versions,\0Aits diagnostic will not be emitted, and no fix will be offered, if `typing_extensions` imports\0Ahave been disabled by the [`lint.typing-extensions`] linter option.\0A\0A## Options\0A\0A- `lint.typing-extensions`\0A", align 1
