@anon.8ad231a129453d088979dfad2582f60a.1204 = private unnamed_addr constant [491 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for classes that only have a public `__init__` method,\0Awithout base classes and decorators.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AClasses with just an `__init__` are possibly better off\0Abeing a dataclass or a namedtuple, which have less boilerplate.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aclass Point:\0A    def __init__(self, x: float, y: float):\0A        self.x = x\0A        self.y = y\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom dataclasses import dataclass\0A\0A\0A@dataclass\0Aclass Point:\0A    x: float\0A    y: float\0A```\0A", align 1
