@anon.8ad231a129453d088979dfad2582f60a.1235 = private unnamed_addr constant [730 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for the attempted use of the unary prefix increment (`++`) or\0Adecrement operator (`--`).\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0APython does not support the unary prefix increment or decrement operator.\0AWriting `++n` is equivalent to `+(+(n))` and writing `--n` is equivalent to\0A`-(-(n))`. In both cases, it is equivalent to `n`.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0A++x\0A--y\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Ax += 1\0Ay -= 1\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: Unary arithmetic and bitwise operations](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/expressions.html#unary-arithmetic-and-bitwise-operations)\0A- [Python documentation: Augmented assignment statements](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/simple_stmts.html#augmented-assignment-statements)\0A", align 1
