@anon.8ad231a129453d088979dfad2582f60a.1325 = private unnamed_addr constant [593 x i8] c"## What it does\0AAdds any required imports, as specified by the user, to the top of the\0Afile.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIn some projects, certain imports are required to be present in all\0Afiles. For example, some projects assume that\0A`from __future__ import annotations` is enabled,\0Aand thus require that import to be\0Apresent in all files. Omitting a \22required\22 import (as specified by\0Athe user) can cause errors or unexpected behavior.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport typing\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom __future__ import annotations\0A\0Aimport typing\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.isort.required-imports`\0A", align 1
