@anon.8ad231a129453d088979dfad2582f60a.1361 = private unnamed_addr constant [1974 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for undocumented public class definitions.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0APublic classes should be documented via docstrings to outline their purpose\0Aand behavior.\0A\0AGenerally, a class docstring should describe the class's purpose and list\0Aits public attributes and methods.\0A\0AIf the codebase adheres to a standard format for class docstrings, follow\0Athat format for consistency.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aclass Player:\0A    def __init__(self, name: str, points: int = 0) -> None:\0A        self.name: str = name\0A        self.points: int = points\0A\0A    def add_points(self, points: int) -> None:\0A        self.points += points\0A```\0A\0AUse instead (in the NumPy docstring format):\0A```python\0Aclass Player:\0A    \22\22\22A player in the game.\0A\0A    Attributes\0A    ----------\0A    name : str\0A        The name of the player.\0A    points : int\0A        The number of points the player has.\0A\0A    Methods\0A    -------\0A    add_points(points: int) -> None\0A        Add points to the player's score.\0A    \22\22\22\0A\0A    def __init__(self, name: str, points: int = 0) -> None:\0A        self.name: str = name\0A        self.points: int = points\0A\0A    def add_points(self, points: int) -> None:\0A        self.points += points\0A```\0A\0AOr (in the Google docstring format):\0A```python\0Aclass Player:\0A    \22\22\22A player in the game.\0A\0A    Attributes:\0A        name: The name of the player.\0A        points: The number of points the player has.\0A    \22\22\22\0A\0A    def __init__(self, name: str, points: int = 0) -> None:\0A        self.name: str = name\0A        self.points: int = points\0A\0A    def add_points(self, points: int) -> None:\0A        self.points += points\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [PEP 257 \E2\80\93 Docstring Conventions](https://peps.python.org/pep-0257/)\0A- [PEP 287 \E2\80\93 reStructuredText Docstring Format](https://peps.python.org/pep-0287/)\0A- [NumPy Style Guide](https://numpydoc.readthedocs.io/en/latest/format.html)\0A- [Google Python Style Guide - Docstrings](https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#38-comments-and-docstrings)\0A", align 1
