@anon.8ad231a129453d088979dfad2582f60a.1365 = private unnamed_addr constant [2038 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for undocumented public method definitions.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0APublic methods should be documented via docstrings to outline their purpose\0Aand behavior.\0A\0AGenerally, a method docstring should describe the method's behavior,\0Aarguments, side effects, exceptions, return values, and any other\0Ainformation that may be relevant to the user.\0A\0AIf the codebase adheres to a standard format for method docstrings, follow\0Athat format for consistency.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aclass Cat(Animal):\0A    def greet(self, happy: bool = True):\0A        if happy:\0A            print(\22Meow!\22)\0A        else:\0A            raise ValueError(\22Tried to greet an unhappy cat.\22)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead (in the NumPy docstring format):\0A```python\0Aclass Cat(Animal):\0A    def greet(self, happy: bool = True):\0A        \22\22\22Print a greeting from the cat.\0A\0A        Parameters\0A        ----------\0A        happy : bool, optional\0A            Whether the cat is happy, is True by default.\0A\0A        Raises\0A        ------\0A        ValueError\0A            If the cat is not happy.\0A        \22\22\22\0A        if happy:\0A            print(\22Meow!\22)\0A        else:\0A            raise ValueError(\22Tried to greet an unhappy cat.\22)\0A```\0A\0AOr (in the Google docstring format):\0A```python\0Aclass Cat(Animal):\0A    def greet(self, happy: bool = True):\0A        \22\22\22Print a greeting from the cat.\0A\0A        Args:\0A            happy: Whether the cat is happy, is True by default.\0A\0A        Raises:\0A            ValueError: If the cat is not happy.\0A        \22\22\22\0A        if happy:\0A            print(\22Meow!\22)\0A        else:\0A            raise ValueError(\22Tried to greet an unhappy cat.\22)\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.pydocstyle.ignore-decorators`\0A\0A## References\0A- [PEP 257 \E2\80\93 Docstring Conventions](https://peps.python.org/pep-0257/)\0A- [PEP 287 \E2\80\93 reStructuredText Docstring Format](https://peps.python.org/pep-0287/)\0A- [NumPy Style Guide](https://numpydoc.readthedocs.io/en/latest/format.html)\0A- [Google Python Style Guide - Docstrings](https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#38-comments-and-docstrings)\0A", align 1
