@anon.8ad231a129453d088979dfad2582f60a.1373 = private unnamed_addr constant [974 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for undocumented public package definitions.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0APublic packages should be documented via docstrings to outline their\0Apurpose and contents.\0A\0AGenerally, package docstrings should list the modules and subpackages that\0Aare exported by the package.\0A\0AIf the codebase adheres to a standard format for package docstrings, follow\0Athat format for consistency.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0A__all__ = [\22Player\22, \22Game\22]\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0A\22\22\22Game and player management package.\0A\0AThis package provides classes for managing players and games.\0A\22\22\22\0A\0A__all__ = [\22player\22, \22game\22]\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [PEP 257 \E2\80\93 Docstring Conventions](https://peps.python.org/pep-0257/)\0A- [PEP 287 \E2\80\93 reStructuredText Docstring Format](https://peps.python.org/pep-0287/)\0A- [NumPy Style Guide](https://numpydoc.readthedocs.io/en/latest/format.html)\0A- [Google Style Python Docstrings](https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#s3.8-comments-and-docstrings)\0A", align 1
