@anon.8ad231a129453d088979dfad2582f60a.1419 = private unnamed_addr constant [723 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `__hash__` implementations that return non-integer values.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe `__hash__` method should return an integer. Returning a different\0Atype may cause unexpected behavior.\0A\0ANote: `bool` is a subclass of `int`, so it's technically valid for `__hash__` to\0Areturn `True` or `False`. However, for consistency with other rules, Ruff will\0Astill emit a diagnostic when `__hash__` returns a `bool`.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aclass Foo:\0A    def __hash__(self):\0A        return \222\22\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aclass Foo:\0A    def __hash__(self):\0A        return 2\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: The `__hash__` method](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/datamodel.html#object.__hash__)\0A", align 1
