@anon.8ad231a129453d088979dfad2582f60a.1442 = private unnamed_addr constant [1241 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for classes with too many public methods\0A\0ABy default, this rule allows up to 20 public methods, as configured by\0Athe [`lint.pylint.max-public-methods`] option.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AClasses with many public methods are harder to understand\0Aand maintain.\0A\0AInstead, consider refactoring the class into separate classes.\0A\0A## Example\0AAssuming that `lint.pylint.max-public-methods` is set to 5:\0A```python\0Aclass Linter:\0A    def __init__(self):\0A        pass\0A\0A    def pylint(self):\0A        pass\0A\0A    def pylint_settings(self):\0A        pass\0A\0A    def flake8(self):\0A        pass\0A\0A    def flake8_settings(self):\0A        pass\0A\0A    def pydocstyle(self):\0A        pass\0A\0A    def pydocstyle_settings(self):\0A        pass\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aclass Linter:\0A    def __init__(self):\0A        self.pylint = Pylint()\0A        self.flake8 = Flake8()\0A        self.pydocstyle = Pydocstyle()\0A\0A    def lint(self):\0A        pass\0A\0A\0Aclass Pylint:\0A    def lint(self):\0A        pass\0A\0A    def settings(self):\0A        pass\0A\0A\0Aclass Flake8:\0A    def lint(self):\0A        pass\0A\0A    def settings(self):\0A        pass\0A\0A\0Aclass Pydocstyle:\0A    def lint(self):\0A        pass\0A\0A    def settings(self):\0A        pass\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.pylint.max-public-methods`\0A", align 1
