@anon.8ad231a129453d088979dfad2582f60a.1485 = private unnamed_addr constant [576 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of `readlines()` when iterating over a file line-by-line.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ARather than iterating over all lines in a file by calling `readlines()`,\0Ait's more convenient and performant to iterate over the file object\0Adirectly.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Awith open(\22file.txt\22) as fp:\0A    for line in fp.readlines():\0A        ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Awith open(\22file.txt\22) as fp:\0A    for line in fp:\0A        ...\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `io.IOBase.readlines`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/io.html#io.IOBase.readlines)\0A", align 1
